Rebuilt QIDI Box modules (qidibox-modules/, MIT, third party)
------------------------------------------------------------

qidibox-modules/ contains compiled Klipper extension binaries (.so) for the
QIDI Box. They are a clean compile of the same stew675 MIT source described
above (see qidibox-modules/build-recipe/SOURCE-MANIFEST.txt for exact inputs
and build environments), produced for CPython 3.12 and CPython 3.7 on aarch64.

These are NOT QIDI's proprietary firmware binaries; no QIDI compiled component
is redistributed. As a compile of the MIT-licensed source, they are covered by
that MIT license, preserved at qidibox-modules/LICENSE. The statement above
that "no QIDI firmware binaries are redistributed" continues to hold: these are
our build of third-party MIT source, not QIDI's binaries.
